sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Baculites compressus at 94.16 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 86.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 closes the three Pass-1 remediation items. The eigenmode step is 0.06 of the diffusion bound instead of 0.12; dispersion Pearson r moves from 0.99966 to 0.99994 and RMSE from 0.00884 to 0.00802 per τ. The comparison-figure caption states that 94.16 µm is the chemical wavelength at the 73.5 Ma Pierre Shale zone, not a caliper reading of the 2.7 cm Bearpaw section. The diffusion sweep stays labeled as a local probe. λ_c remains 94.16 µm, λ_max 96.54 µm, and equal diffusion still decays. The flank GIF is unchanged in construction: 12 frames, 720×480. Overall 86.1/100 (faithfulness 85.0, reproducibility 88.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8f0ebbb7583b60dab933158a86eda8e291baab3e; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8f0ebbb7583b60dab933158a86eda8e291baab3e, image/png, 360713 B, 1512×888 px, artifact_sha256 82db17e1563506663b44dd1014ffe0e9552def2e009d7c36168ca95d436134cf (sha256 82db17e1563506663b44dd1014ffe0e9552def2e009d7c36168ca95d436134cf), spec_fingerprint 987c95abfd36be5a754c6bd9b1cc8b19b4c29acfc2ed8558194b88bb00b620d6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 987c95abfd36be5a754c6bd9b1cc8b19b4c29acfc2ed8558194b88bb00b620d6; artifact_sha256: 82db17e1563506663b44dd1014ffe0e9552def2e009d7c36168ca95d436134cf; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0/baculites_compressus_specimen.jpg=b4eabd655977c5ee..., datasets/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=1e794dec0e5bf0ec..., datasets/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=03254933877482eb...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and the inhibitor-long-range instability. | Schnakenberg (1979) trimolecular steady state u0=a+b, v0=b/(a+b)^2. | Meinhardt & Klingler (1987): mollusc pigment records a mantle-edge reaction-diffusion system. | G. C. C. (1892): Baculites compressus has a coiled early stage before the orthoconic shaft. | Fatherree, Harries & Quinn (1998): B. compressus in the upper Campanian Pierre Shale of South Dakota.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u solved so the k_c formula returns λ_c = 94.16 µm at r = 9.2 and χ = 1. | Numeric σ(k) at the tightened timestep, and the equal-diffusion ablation. | χ readout 3/2 and 6215/9416 for the predecessor and successor. | Flank mode packet, foreground segmentation, and the figure caption's formation transfer.; transfer_boundary: The photograph is a Bearpaw Formation section; the age anchor 73.5 Ma is the Pierre Shale zone. The figure caption says so. | Shell-pigment RD is transferred from gastropod models to an ammonite mantle.; does_not_claim: 94.16 µm was not measured on the photograph. | χ for Placenticeras and Nipponites is not a fossil pigment measurement. | The Wikimedia caption age of 100 Ma is not used. | The flank GIF is not a 2D integration of the PDE on the shell mesh.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'One polished Bearpaw section stands in for a Pierre Shale population. χ for Placenticeras and Nipponites is still a geometric prediction, and the flank GIF is still not a 2D shell-mesh integration.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.861"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

